  "public_contract": [
    "Native full-word register/return APIs are preserved.",
    "SDK callback adapters implement the pinned uint8-register/int8-return signatures and two-argument void delay type.",
    "Delay adapter ignores the SDK interface pointer and calls the one-argument native delay; FIFO now declares and calls the same signature.",
    "Callback pointer targets differ from the old alias registration and are normalized by semantic role in stock comparisons."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Physical sensor/bus behavior, timing and final application linking/startup unverified.",
    "Bus results and cycle primitive modeled; modeled reads deliver at most sixteen bytes to test adapter forwarding.",
    "FIFO regression models its lower power/read/log/delay services.",
    "Native full allocation extent remains a separate gate; only the pinned 52-byte C context is checked.",
    "Incidental R1/void-delay return/APSR, faults/concurrency, provider overruns and byte identity excluded.",
    "Architecture-specific shared delay implementation remains unchanged outside native BMA runtime units."
  ],
